d","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Rhizopus is a genus of common saprophytic fungi on plants and  specialized parasites on animals. They are found in a wide variety of organic substances, including \"mature fruits and vegetables\", jellies, syrups, leather, bread, peanuts, and tobacco. They are multicellular. Some Rhizopus species are opportunistic human pathogens that often cause fatal disease called mucormycosis. This widespread genus includes at least eight species."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-rhizopus"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhizopus"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Tempeh","dish/tempeh"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Acetic acid","ingredient/acetic-acid"],["Rhizopus oligosporus","ingredient/rhizopus-oligosporus"],["Soybean","ingredient/soybean"]]}]},"dish/the-stinking-rose":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/the-stinking-rose","n":"The Stinking Rose","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["The Stinking Rose is a Californian restaurant known for including garlic in all its dishes, including its garlic ice cream. The first location opened in  San Francisco in 1991, followed by a second location in Beverly Hills in 1996.  The Beverly Hills restaurant announced its permanent closure in October 2021. The San Francisco location was originally located at 325 Columbus Ave, and moved in 2021 to its current address at 430 Columbus Avenue, in the heart of San Francisco's North Beach neighborhood."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-the-stinking-rose"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Stinking_Rose"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","ref":"sit