occa-di-lupo"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Bombolone","dish/bombolone"],["Buca di Beppo","dish/buca-di-beppo"],["Budino","dish/budino"],["Buona","dish/buona"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Caffé Vittoria","dish/caffe-vittoria"],["Camille's (Providence, Rhode Island)","dish/camille-s-providence-rhode-island"],["Campisi's Egyptian Restaurant","dish/campisi-s-egyptian-restaurant"],["Cannelloni","dish/cannelloni"],["Capellini","dish/capellini"]]}]},"dish/frybread":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/frybread","n":"Frybread","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 4 cuisines","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Frybread comes out of hunger. When the U.S. government forced the ",["Diné","cuisine/dine-foodways"]," on the Long Walk to land that couldn't support their crops, and pushed other nations off their homelands, it handed out rations of white flour, lard, sugar and salt. Fried dough from those rations kept families alive."],["Today it's a powwow staple and the base of Indian tacos, and it holds both pride and pain: a sign of survival, and a reminder of the foods that were lost. It's also high in fat and calories. Some critics tie it to diabetes on reservations, while others say the deeper problem is access to healthy food, and many communities are bringing traditional foods back alongside it."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"Smithsonian Magazine, Frybread","url":"https://www.smithsonianmag.com/arts-culture/frybread-79191/"},{"name":"Washington State Health Care Authority, Food and survival","url":"https://connections.hca.wa.gov/hca/2025/november/food-and-survival-why-fry-bread-is-not-a-novelty-food"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-frybread"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frybread"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Diné foodways","cuisine/dine-foodways"],["Lakota foodways","cuisine/lakota-foodways"],["Cherokee foodways","cuisine/cherokee-foodways"],["Native American cuisine","cuisine/native-american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Lard","ingredient/lard"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Owamni","ref":"site/owamni-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"owamni.com","note":"Sean Sherman's Minneapolis restaurant, cooking only with Indigenous ingredients.","url":"https://owamni.com/","suggested":true},{"name":"Cherokee Tribal Food Distribution Program","ref":"site/food-ebci-nsn-gov","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"food.ebci-nsn.gov","note":"Traditional recipes from the Eastern Band of Cherokee Indians, like Three Sisters stew and chestnut bread.","url":"https://food.ebci-nsn.gov/?p=4673","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Diné foodways","links":[["Blue corn mush","dish/blue-corn-mush"],["Kneel down bread","dish/kneel-down-bread"]]},{"h":"Mentioned in","links":[["Wojapi","dish/wojapi"]]}]},"cookbook/british-regional-food":{"t":"book","r":"cookbook/british-regional-food","n":"British Regional Food","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Cookbooks","cookbooks"]],"sub":"Cookbook by Mark Hix, 2006","square":true,"suggested":true,"isbn":"9781844002344","intro":[["London chef Mark Hix's survey of regional dishes and producers across Britain."]],"actions":[{"kind":"out","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9781844002344","label":"Open Library"}],"sections":[{"h":"Cuisines it covers","count":1,"links":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine"]]}]}}